@node fir-designer Plugin Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

FIR magnitude and phase designer with parametric target bands.

@subsubheading What It Does

A FIR (Finite Impulse Response) equalizer that turns parametric target bands into a designed FIR response. It can run as a linear-phase EQ for phase-coherent work, or as a minimum-phase FIR when lower perceived latency is more important.

@subsubheading Features

@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{Phase mode}: Linear or minimum-phase FIR design
@item @strong{FIR convolution}: Uses frequency-domain convolution for efficient processing
@item @strong{Parametric bands}: Standard frequency, Q, and gain controls
@item @strong{High precision}: Ideal for mastering and critical listening
@item @strong{Auto Gain}: Normalizes the FIR's DC gain to unity. It is a predictable
@end itemize

  reference-point correction, not a perceptual loudness match.

